INSERT INTO biochar_news (title, chunk_text, url, embedding, publish_date) VALUES ('UK Biochar Research Centre | Welcome to the UKBRC', '1 September 2024
The State of Carbon Dioxide Removal Report – Second Edition Released
The Second Edition of the
State of Carbon Dioxide Removal
report was published on 4 June, highlighting the urgent need to scale up Carbon Dioxide Removal (CDR) methods to meet global climate targets. The report emphasises that 7–9 billion tonnes of CO2 per year will need to be removed from the atmosphere by mid-century to achieve the 1.5°C Paris Agreement target.
Among novel CDR methods, biochar stands out as the major player, contributing significantly to carbon removal efforts. Its versatility and effectiveness in applications such as soil enhancement, construction materials, and environmental remediation position biochar as a key technology in the global CDR portfolio.
