incinerate animal carcasses with a capacity of over 10 tonnes per day, they’ll require a Part A(2) environmental permit from their local authority.
Best available techniques
( BAT ) only applies to
SWIPs
in England if they are
subject to Part B requirements .
4.1 Small waste oil burners
SWOBs
are appliances used to burn waste oil.
Waste oil
is any mineral, synthetic lubrication or industrial oils that have become unfit for the use for which they were originally intended. For example:
combustion engine (eg petrol or diesel) oils and gearbox oils
lubricating oils
hydraulic oils
Waste oils that haven’t
met the end-of-waste criteria for the production and use of processed fuel oil
are classed as waste.
SWOBs
are considered to be
