Integrate
trees, shrubs , and
perennial
plants to increase
woody biomass
and carbon stored below and above ground.
Managed/Rotational Grazing
Move livestock on
planned rest periods
to maximize
root growth ,
soil carbon input , and minimize overgrazing.
Enhanced Nutrient Stewardship
Apply fertilizers in sync with
crop demand
to optimize nitrogen use, limit emissions, and promote root-driven carbon sequestration.
Organic Amendments (Compost, Biochar, Manure)
Add stable carbon-rich residues to
build soil matter , improve biology, and increase long-term carbon stabilization.
Baseline Assessment and Ongoing MRV
Establish a starting point, use periodic
measurement
(including
remote sensing ), and perform
verification
to ensure credible emission reductions.
