MRV
for carbon offsets typically includes:
Soil carbon sampling : Field-based soil cores, lab analysis for organic matter.
Remote sensing : Multispectral satellite imagery (like what
Farmonaut
provides) to monitor vegetation indexes, track biomass, and document
land use changes .
Modeling : Predicting
carbon sequestration pathways
based on crop, geography, and practice data.
Field surveys : Reporting on practice use, residue cover, and tillage methods.
Blockchain-based data traceability : Ensures transparency, builds trust, and facilitates auditing across
supply chains .
Permanence
(stored carbon stays in place) and
additionality
(sequestration exceeds business as usual) are crucial. Credible
