INSERT INTO biochar_news (title, chunk_text, url, embedding, publish_date) VALUES ('Trend watch: Soil carbon MRV & incentives in 2026 — signals, win…', 'nts Pilot programs in 12 US states Scaling through USDA and state programs Multiple revenue streams improve farmer economics and program retention
Red Flags
Rising farmer attrition rates in voluntary carbon programs.
Early reports from multi-year soil carbon programs show 15-25% of enrolled farmers declining to re-enroll after their initial contract period. Reasons include insufficient payment relative to practice costs, excessive data reporting requirements, and frustration with delayed credit issuance. If attrition accelerates, programs will struggle to demonstrate the long-term practice adoption required for durable sequestration.
