Brussels publishes corrected CBAM default values which could impact EU importers 2026 costs
The European Commission has published corrected country-level emissions default values under the Carbon Border Adjustment Mechanism (CBAM), which could have a significant impact on CBAM costs for EU importers of certain products in 2026.
Spanish low-carbon steel project secures €150 mln investment commitment
A planned low-carbon steel plant in central Spain has secured a €150 million investment commitment from a fund managed by development finance institution COFIDES, its developer announced Wednesday.
