BRIEFING: Italy’s recycling success could become key argument against waste inclusion in ETS
Italy looks set to rely on one if its strongest environmental credentials – its strong recycling performance – to escape the European Commission’s proposal to bring municipal waste incineration into the EU Emissions Trading System (ETS).
German environment ministry reshuffle puts international work at its core
Germany’s Ministry for the Environment, Nature Conservation, Nuclear Safety, and Consumer Protection (BMUKN) is reshuffling its offices, with the aim for better integrating international affairs work, according to German media.
