Climate-driven forest damage threatens EU carbon sink as biomass losses accelerate
Europe’s forests have suffered a sharp acceleration in biomass losses since 2018 as climate-driven disturbances intensify, threatening the continent’s ability to use forests as a key natural carbon sink despite policies aimed at increasing carbon removals by 2030, according to a new study.
Euro Markets: EUAs remain rangebound as efforts to test extremes fall short in thin trade
European carbon prices ended Wednesday little changed after falling to their lowest in more than two weeks and bouncing back strongly as traders found the market’s appetite for volatility rather lacking.
