Brussels model for integrating DACCS into EU ETS uses old data, claims expert
The European Commission (EC) has come under further criticism for its plans to integrate carbon dioxide removal (CDR) credits into the EU ETS, after a policy expert claimed the pricing model for direct air capture with carbon storage (DACCS) relies on a single source with  vague data from 2023.
Great British Energy backs renewable heating tech, to decarbonise commercial buildings
The UK’s publicly owned Great British Energy is putting £7.5 million into a solar thermal energy developer, which it believes can help to accelerate emission cuts from heating.
