INTERVIEW: Latin America stands out for forest business potential, but demand lags
Latin America’s comparatively developed financial markets, regulations, and institutions have made it a favourable environment for forest businesses, but many biodiversity-based products still lack the consistent demand needed to reach commercial scale, according to a regional director at a UK-funded programme.
