An Indian carbon project developer has shelved plans to expand its domestic improved cookstove programme and is considering neighbouring country Nepal for its next project, as tighter carbon accounting rules reduce issuance and buyers favour higher-integrity units.
New coal power plants entering operation in China reach 10-year high in H1 2026, report says
New coal power plants entering operation in China reached the highest first half of the year level since 2016, despite a policy shift signalling stricter controls on new approvals, according to a report.
