Indian textile body inks pact with global cotton forum for regenerative farming, carbon credit generation
India’s apex industry chamber representing the textile and clothing sector has signed an agreement with the global cotton body to develop projects based on regenerative agricultural practices, it said.
Sustainability-linked loans flowed to palm oil firms facing deforestation allegations in Indonesia -report
Major financial institutions arranged $31 billion in sustainability-linked loans (SLLs) between 2018-25 to palm oil companies reportedly tied to deforestation in Indonesia, said non-profit Global Witness.
