INSERT INTO biochar_news (title, chunk_text, url, embedding, publish_date) VALUES ('Voluntary Carbon Market News: August 3-9, 2026', 'company''s existing carbon credit project in Maine. Acadian''s financial results for Q2 showed profitability on its Maine operations and reduced sales in New Brunswick, according to Interim President and CEO Malcolm Cockwell, adding that it expects Maine projects to continue delivering profits in the remainder of the year, and New Brunswick to return to normal harvesting levels. Overall, Acadian''s Q2 2026 timber sales dropped from the previous year, down to C$14.6 mln ($10.4 mln), and net income fell from $2.7 mln in Q2 2025 to $1.3 mln in Q2 2026. Free Cash Flow dropped significantly from the previous year, from $777,000 to $224,000.
