INSERT INTO biochar_news (title, chunk_text, url, embedding, publish_date) VALUES ('Behind Veolia’s Next-Gen Carbon Capture System in Sheffield', ' to operate continuously without constantly replenishing the chemical. At this stage the captured CO₂ is being released again as part of the testing process, rather than stored or put to use.  Once the concept has been proven the plan is to make use of that carbon, though the trial is expected to last around two years.
Veolia and Sheffield City Council say that the trial is intended to establish whether the technology is economically viable to scale up.
For Greg Searle, the Commercial Director at C-Capture, this trial is “a major milestone”.
“It demonstrates not only the scalability of our non‑amine approach, but also its real‑world advantages in energy efficiency, cost, and safety – particularly for challenging applications like energy-from-waste facilities,” he explains.
