INSERT INTO biochar_news (title, chunk_text, url, embedding, publish_date) VALUES ('Behind Veolia’s Next-Gen Carbon Capture System in Sheffield', 'CCS systems located in the North Sea. The Acorn Project: Acorn is Scotland’s only advanced CCS project as things stand. New investments will see old oil and gas pipelines from North Sea rigs repurposed to transport carbon emissions to storage sites in the ocean. Viking CCS: This project, led by Harbour Energy and bp, is also located in Humberside. It will use underground pipelines to move carbon emissions to the old Theddlethorpe Gas Terminal, where it is expected that around 10 million tonnes of CO₂ could be stored by 2035. However, Veolia points out that more than half of the UK''s emissions occur outside these clusters, meaning that inland assets, like the company’s plant in Sheffield, currently sit outside the main funding architecture. As such,
Veolia
