INSERT INTO biochar_news (title, chunk_text, url, embedding, publish_date) VALUES ('Pragmatism drives MENA’s waste conversion industries', 'state services and resource efficiency.
Here again, economic concerns are driving adoption. Oman is a small country where only around 4.6% of the total land area is suitable for cultivation. Meanwhile, approximately 80% is classified as desert or semi-desert. In this context, it is vital to protect water and soils from toxic wastestreams.
The country has no shortage of waste feedstock to work with: 3.1 million tonnes were deposited in engineered landfills in 2024. With an expanding population, this is a problem (and a resource pool) that will only grow.
