INSERT INTO biochar_news (title, chunk_text, url, embedding, publish_date) VALUES ('Tracking the Next Wave of State Food Waste Policy in 2026', 'egory descriptions to better reflect the types of legislation we’re seeing and put bills in multiple categories when they have more than one intended purpose.
As of July 2026, 37 states have introduced 135 unique bills related to food waste, with 26 enacted so far this year. Of the remaining bills, 45 are still pending, and 64 are now dead, meaning the bill can no longer pass. New Jersey and New York lead with 21 unique bills introduced by legislators in each of those states, followed by California with 16.”
To read the full story, visit
https://refed.org/articles/tracking-the-next-wave-of-state-food-waste-policy-in-2026/ .
Author: Heather Latino, Harvard Law School Food Law and Policy Clinic, ReFED
